# ==============================================================================
# MarketPulse Frontend — Production Environment Variables
# ==============================================================================
#
# VITE_API_URL and VITE_SOCKET_URL are NOT required in production.
#
# In production, the Nginx reverse proxy handles all routing:
#   - REST API calls  (/api/*)       → proxied to backend:5000 internally
#   - WebSocket calls (/socket.io/)  → proxied to backend:5000 with WS upgrade
#
# The frontend uses:
#   - api.ts:           baseURL = "" (same-origin relative paths)
#   - SocketContext.tsx: window.location.origin (resolves at runtime in browser)
#
# Port 5000 does NOT need to be open in the AWS Security Group.
# Only port 80 (and 443 if using HTTPS) need to be publicly accessible.
#
# For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT, frontend/.env is used:
#   VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
#   VITE_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:5000
